# The story idle-compact was made for, in five scenes, over a graph of how big the conversation is.
title:   Use Claude Code in the cloud without paying to re-read a big conversation
caption: You work with Claude in a cloud session. The conversation gets large, you stop for a while, and the prompt cache expires. idle-compact compacts the conversation while you are away, so your next message reads a short summary instead of the whole conversation without the cache.
note:    Compacting replaces the details of the old conversation with a summary. This story is for when that trade is fine with you; if it is not, raise the thresholds or switch the mod off.

# scene  <icon>  <hue>  <size from>-<size to>  <title> — <text>      sizes are percent of the graph's height
scene  cloud    blue    6-40    You use Claude Code in the cloud — You work with Claude in a cloud session.
scene  grow     teal    40-86   The conversation gets large — Every message, file and reply is added to the context. It reaches about 150k tokens. The cache keeps each new message cheap.
scene  away     mute    86-86   You stop; the cache expires — You stop working for a while. The cache expires.
scene  compact  green   86-10   idle-compact compacts it — After 20 minutes without a turn, idle-compact runs /compact. The conversation is replaced by a short summary.
scene  back     green   10-16   You come back to a small context — Your next message reads the summary, not 150k uncached tokens. It is faster and cheaper.

graph    Context size — what every message costs to read
away     3 4  you are away
with     with idle-compact
without  without it: your next message re-reads about 150k tokens, uncached

term  Cloud session — Claude Code running on a remote machine that you reach from the web or your phone. Claude Code's own idle compaction is switched off there, which is why idle-compact exists.
term  Context window — everything Claude reads to answer you: the whole conversation so far. It is measured in tokens; a token is roughly three quarters of a word.
term  Cache — while you are actively working, Claude Code keeps the conversation cached, so each new message only pays for what is new. After a pause the cache expires (a "cache miss"), and the next message pays for the entire conversation again.
term  Compact — replace the conversation so far with a short summary of it and carry on from there. Details that are not in the summary are gone from Claude's view.
